# PART 6 — INDIVIDUAL WORD PRONUNCIATION

## 26. CLICK-TO-PRONOUNCE

The user must be able to click ANY individual German word in the displayed text.

This action is separate from the normal reading mode.

When the user clicks a word:

1. Pause the current sentence or continuous playback.
2. Identify exactly which word was selected.
3. Generate or retrieve audio for that word.
4. Pronounce ONLY the selected word.
5. Do not read the full sentence.
6. Do not read neighboring words.
7. Use the same selected German female voice.
8. Return to the previous reading position after word playback.

Example:

Displayed sentence:

„Ich lerne Deutsch, weil ich in Deutschland arbeiten möchte.“

If the user clicks:

arbeiten

The audio must pronounce only:

„arbeiten“

It must NOT pronounce:

„Ich lerne Deutsch ...“

It must NOT read the complete sentence.

## 27. WORD INTERACTION

Every German word must be independently clickable.

Provide:
- Hover effect.
- Click effect.
- Selected word highlight.
- Pronunciation playback.
- Vocabulary popup.

Do not require users to select the entire sentence before selecting a word.

The word selection must work with:
- Normal paragraphs.
- Long texts.
- Quoted passages.
- Dialogues.
- Punctuation.
- Words with German umlauts.
- Compound words.

Ignore punctuation when identifying the pronunciation target.

## 28. WORD PLAYBACK SETTINGS

When the word is clicked:

- Pause current reading.
- Pronounce selected word only.
- Keep the current sentence position.
- Return to the paused state after pronunciation.
- Allow Resume.

